  "format": "batch-draw@1",
  "about": "The draw of a batch accepted on a sample (specs/attestation/batch.md §3). seed = SHA-256(\"kash-batch-draw-v1\\n\" ‖ seal digest ‖ block hash), the hash as Bitcoin displays it. The stream is SHA-256(seed ‖ n) for n = 0, 1, 2, … as four big-endian bytes, each block read as four big-endian 64-bit words. A number below m takes the next word w and gives w mod m when w is below 2^64 − (2^64 mod m), else takes the next word. The positions: for i = 0 … sample−1, j = i + (a number below size − i), swap entries i and j of 0 … size−1; the first `sample` entries, ascending. Reference: @kashscript/attest/batch's drawSeed and drawPositions.",
